e the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe line parameterized by\n\\[\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\]lies in a plane of the form $x + y + cz = d.$  Enter the ordered pair $(c,d).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"85b1c0e331e0ed798c0aaa2afa1023706b9842ceaf3f9ed294ff88558bb5b7c1"},"seconds":25.21892476081848,"seed":472890987638002492,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by identifying the line parameterized by \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) and the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\). The parameterized line is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nFrom this, we can express the coordinates \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) in terms of the parameter \\(t\\):\n\\[\nx = 1 + t, \\quad y = 3t, \\quad z = 1 - t\n\\]\n\nWe substitute these expressions into the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\):\n\\[\n(1 + t) + 3t + c(1 - t) = d\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side of the equation:\n\\[\n1 + t + 3t + c - ct = d\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + 4t + c - ct = d\n\\]\nCombine like terms involving \\(t\\):\n\\[\n1 + c + t(4 - c) = d\n\\]\n\nFor the line to lie in the plane, the equation must hold for all values of \\(t\\). This implies that the coefficient of \\(t\\) must be zero and the constant term must match \\(d\\). Therefore, we set up the following system of equations:\n\\[\n4 - c = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + c = d\n\\]\n\nSolve the first equation for \\(c\\):\n\\[\n4 - c = 0 \\implies c = 4\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(c = 4\\) into the second equation to find \\(d\\):\n\\[\n1 + 4 = d \\implies d = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(4, 5)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(4, 5)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
